    "_note_bareModifiers": "combination is the canonical bare-modifier name. Left+right pairs map to a Double* name via the bare-modifier table (NOT the modifier pressed), which is what the label formatter renders as ⌘ + ⌘ and what the skip set uses to avoid the input-monitoring prompt. Fn alone is bare via that table. The `bare` flag is macOS-gated; combination is not, so Ctrl+Alt has a combination on Windows too but bare=false there."
